\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord of the worlds above,
\par How pleasant and how fair
\par The dwellings of Thy love,
\par Thine earthly temples, are!
\par To Thine abode
\par My heart aspires
\par With warm desires
\par To see my God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O happy souls that pray
\par Where God dlights to hear!
\par O happy men that pay
\par Their constant service there!
\par They praise Thee still,
\par And happy they
\par Who love the way
\par To Zion's hill!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. They go from strength to strength,
\par Through this dark vale of tears,
\par Till each o'ercomes at length,
\par Till each in heaven appears:
\par O glorious seat!
\par Thou God, our King,
\par Shalt thither bring
\par Our willing feet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. God is our sun and shield,
\par Our light and our defence;
\par With gifts His hands are filled,
\par We draw our blessings thence:
\par He shall bestow
\par Upon our race
\par His saving grace,
\par And glory too.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The Lord His people loves;
\par His hands no good withholds
\par From those His hearts approves,
\par From holy, humble souls:
\par Thrice happy he,
\par O Lord of Hosts,
\par Whose spirit trusts
\par Alone in Thee!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

